    {
      "id": "UgxlgRoa_jCpzb5UI1h4AaABAg",
      "author": "@jewelmorgan6315",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/BY5F6S67Y_fMu4jn0zmKufq8yzgBdZg9K3fKlxv9lj0pvoOqo0QlBShlmK_oddzj-aKCN2nk=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Watching from the Netherlands It's really funny to see how a foreign filmmaker looks at us. Things that are very common to us like riding a bike, or the word \"gezelligheid\" or our way of direct communication.  \nIt is however not completely accurate. The reason why the housing have become more difficult is also due to Airbnb that made normal houses suddenly just available for tourists, and city halls loving the idea of more tourist tax and to support the economy to allow more recreation homes, then normal houses. There are hectares of holiday parcs entirely empty from autumn till summer where people could live, but are not allowed. \nAnother factor is the incredible amount of people coming from other countries to work in the Netherlands. As it is very hard to find good staff, or even youngsters willing to work, people from Portugal, Poland or other countries come to work in the hospitality business or other. They too need a roof over their heads. This same housing situation we see in Spain and Ibiza where people buy houses just to have their holidays in, making it impossible for the habitants to find a home. \nAlso what you state about us talking things through... nahhh we are not the saint we may seem ;-) There is a lot of indifferences as well, and we are always so busy, always a full calendar, very much on our own as well, that we often do not take the time to talk things through. \n\n\nPs what was the dark secret again? Nice title to draw in viewers ;-) or is this too direct? ;-)",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-23T11:15:22Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
    },
    {
